  "slug": "sequences-promoter-38cf",
  "summary": "Deep-learning structure predictors are being benchmarked on RNA and protein-RNA complexes, exposing accuracy limits on novel RNA folds.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is computational prediction and assessment of RNA structure, binding, and interfaces. DUET predicts RNA-small molecule binding sites from sequence alone using a relational graph tower and frozen RNA language model convolutions. ScanFold3 accelerates RNA secondary structure scanning for structured targets in genomes and transcriptomes, reporting 38-129x gains over ScanFold2 on long sequences. A validation approach extends conkit-validate to RNA, comparing predicted contact patterns from deep-learning predictors against deposited structures. An AlphaFold 3 evaluation across more than 1,300 protein-RNA complexes and about 270 RNA-only systems finds fold and interface accuracy declining on novel RNAs. CryoID2 applies 3D U-Net analysis to cryoEM maps to identify protein and RNA candidates. What is new is the shift toward testing deep-learning RNA predictions against deposited structures and novel folds, not only generating them.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-haiku-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-04"
}
